<description>
Recolor every black 5-cell plus whose center and four orthogonal neighbors are black to green.

Input structure:
- The grid contains only black and teal pixels.
- Some black pixels are centers of a full black orthogonal cross.
- Teal pixels are fixed blockers and are never recolored.

Rule:
- Find every black pixel whose north, south, west, and east neighbors are also black.
- For each such center, recolor the center and its four orthogonal neighbors green.
- Overlapping pluses simply merge into one green mask.

Key insight:
- The longer marked shapes are not separate templates; they are unions of adjacent black pluses.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "black pixels in a binary black/teal grid",
  "transform": "recolor to green every black pixel that is the center or orthogonal neighbor of a full black 5-cell plus; preserve all teal pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 12x12 [observed]
  colors: input uses only BLACK and TEAL; output adds GREEN
  background: ~50% TEAL pixels scattered randomly (no pattern), 39-52% BLACK
  plus_centers:
    count: 2-5 black pixels whose 4 orthogonal neighbors are also black
    position: rows 1-10, cols 1-10 (need 1-cell margin for arms)
    groups: 1-3 connected components where centers within L1 dist <=2 merge
    group_size: 1-2 centers per group
    inter_group_distance: >=5 L1
  near_plus_distractors: 8-12 black pixels with exactly 3/4 orthogonal black neighbors [observed]
  transform:
    rule: recolor each plus center and its 4 arms from BLACK to GREEN
    overlapping pluses merge into one green region

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Create 12x12 grid filled with TEAL.
    2. Choose 2-5 plus centers (rows 1-10, cols 1-10). Group them into 1-3
       clusters; within a cluster, centers are L1 dist 1-2 apart; between
       clusters, >=5 apart.
    3. Mark each center and its 4 arms as GREEN (the output state).
    4. Scatter additional BLACK pixels randomly across remaining TEAL cells
       until ~40-52% of the grid is BLACK+GREEN. Ensure no accidental new
       plus centers form (check each newly placed black pixel and its neighbors).
    5. Output grid = current grid. Input grid = copy with all GREEN replaced
       by BLACK.
```
